","type":"text/x-markdown"},"/home/runner/work/tw-plugin-library/tw-plugin-library/wiki/plugins/rimir/streams-extras/README.md":{"title":"/home/runner/work/tw-plugin-library/tw-plugin-library/wiki/plugins/rimir/streams-extras/README.md","text":"# rimir/streams-extras

UX extensions for the [sq/streams](https://github.com/saqimtiaz/streams) TiddlyWiki plugin. Adds a cascading **Copy ▸** / **Paste ▸** menu to the streams right-click contextmenu.

## What it does

- **Copy ▸ Structure** — captures the right-clicked node + its descendants (titles, text, hierarchy) into a wiki state tiddler. Round-trips losslessly via Paste ▸ Structure.
- **Copy ▸ TW-List / MD-List / HTML-List** — flat outline of the subtree to the system clipboard in the chosen format.
- **Paste ▸ Structure** — recreate the captured subtree as a new child of the right-clicked node. Disabled if nothing copied.
- **Paste ▸ Text-List** — read the clipboard, auto-detect TW / MD / HTML, parse, create matching children under the target.

Every newly-pasted node from a structure paste carries an `orig-tiddler` field pointing at its source title.

## Programmatic flatten

Beyond the contextmenu, the plugin exposes `$action-streams-flatten-inplace` (attrs: `node`, `format` = `tw` | `md` | `html`, default `tw`). Destructive: renders the subtree as a flat outline, appends to `node`'s text, drops `stream-list` + `stream-type`, flips `note-type: streams → text`, then deletes every descendant node. Used by `rimir/orga-apps`' Hygiene panel to freeze completed streams-notes.

## How it works

Shadow override of `$:/plugins/sq/streams/contextmenu/contextmenu-template` with cascading-mode rendering. The cascade-trigger entries (Copy ▸ / Paste ▸) are wrapped in `<div class="tc-popup-keep">` so the click that flips the mode doesn't dismiss the popup — the same popup re-renders into the sub-menu in place. `plugin-priority: 2` so this override wins shadow precedence over the priority-1 streams plugin.

## Prerequisites

- TiddlyWiki ≥ 5.4.0
- `sq/streams` ≥ 1.2.24

