|!Version |!Date |!Changes |
|0.1.1 |2026-05-21 |New ''$action-streams-flatten-inplace'' widget — destructive in-place flattening of a streams-node subtree. Renders the descendants of `node` as a flat outline in the chosen `format` (`"tw"` | `"md"` | `"html"`, default `"tw"`), appends to `node`'s text (joined with `\n\n` if `node` already has text, otherwise replaces), drops the `stream-list` + `stream-type` fields, flips `note-type: streams → text` so the streams ViewTemplate stops handling the parent, and finally walks the subtree leaf-up deleting every descendant node tiddler (leaf-up so we don't dangle `stream-list` references during the pass). Built for `rimir/orga-apps` 0.2.77's new Hygiene panel ''🪄 Flatten'' button — the per-note clean-up flow that turns a streams-shaped note into a plain text/markdown/HTML one once a meeting/project is "done" and the live editing structure is no longer needed. ''Implementation'': reuses the existing `walkTW` / `walkMD` / `walkHTML` walkers via a new shared `renderChildrenFlat(rootNode, format)` helper — same per-format output rules as `$action-streams-copy-list`, just starting at the root's children instead of the root itself. ''Refactor pass'' on the existing render functions: the original `renderTW` / `renderMD` / `renderHTML` each had its own private `walk` IIFE; the new flatten action would've duplicated those walks again (the first draft did exactly that — ~25 lines of copy-paste). Hoisted the walkers to module scope so `renderTW`/`renderMD`/`renderHTML` and `renderChildrenFlat` all share them. `renderTW` and `renderMD` now thread the accumulator explicitly as `out` instead of closing over it, since module-scope walkers can't access a per-call array via closure. |
|0.1.0 |2026-05-19 |''Initial release.'' Spun out of `rimir/mindmap` 0.2.32 — the contextmenu Copy/Paste cascade has no real relationship to mindmap and belonged in its own plugin. Same functional surface as the mindmap 0.2.32 build: shadow override of `$:/plugins/sq/streams/contextmenu/contextmenu-template` adds cascading ''`Copy ▸`'' (Structure / TW-List / MD-List / HTML-List) and ''`Paste ▸`'' (Structure / Text-List) entries with `tc-popup-keep` wrappers so the cascade-trigger clicks don't dismiss the popup. Override of `oncontext-menu-actions` (via `$:/tags/streams/user-actionmacros`) clears the cascade-mode field on each fresh right-click. Four JS action widgets (`$action-streams-copy-*`, `$action-streams-paste-*`) implement the serialize / render / parse / create logic. Pasted nodes carry an `orig-tiddler` lineage stamp (omitted for clipboard pastes). `plugin-priority: 2` so this override wins precedence over the priority-1 streams plugin in TW's `unpackPluginTiddlers` iteration. Tiddler titles renamespaced to `$:/plugins/rimir/streams-extras/*` (state tiddler at `$:/state/rimir/streams-extras/clipboard/structure` was already in this namespace and didn't move). |
