Adds a cascading ''Copy ▸'' / ''Paste ▸'' menu to the right-click contextmenu of any [[sq/streams|$:/plugins/sq/streams]] node. The two cascades are:

;Copy ▸
:* ''Structure'' — captures the node + its descendants into a wiki state tiddler. Round-trips losslessly via Paste ▸ Structure.
:* ''TW-List'' — flat outline in TiddlyWiki syntax (`*`, `**`, `***` …) to the system clipboard.
:* ''MD-List'' — Markdown indented `- ` outline to the system clipboard.
:* ''HTML-List'' — nested `<ul><li>` outline to the system clipboard.

;Paste ▸
:* ''Structure'' — recreate the captured subtree as a new child of the right-clicked node. Disabled if nothing has been copied.
:* ''Text-List'' — read the clipboard, auto-detect TW / MD / HTML, parse, create matching children under the target.

! Lineage

Every newly-pasted stream node from a ''structure'' paste carries an `orig-tiddler` field pointing at its source title — so you always know where a duplicated subtree came from. Clipboard pastes have no source tiddler to record and the field stays off.

! Flatten in-place (programmatic)

Beyond the contextmenu, the plugin also exposes `$action-streams-flatten-inplace` (attrs: `node`, `format` = `tw` | `md` | `html`, default `tw`). Destructive: renders the subtree of `node` as a flat outline, appends to `node`'s text, drops `stream-list` + `stream-type` fields, flips `note-type: streams → text`, then deletes every descendant. Built for callers that need to "freeze" a streams-note into a plain text/markdown/HTML one (e.g. `rimir/orga-apps`' Hygiene panel uses it to clean up streams-notes from completed entities).

! Why a separate plugin?

The Copy/Paste cascade was originally part of `rimir/mindmap` (a streams-aware preview pane is where the user encountered streams nodes most). But the contextmenu integration applies to streams ''anywhere'' it renders, has no real relationship to mindmaps, and shadowing a `$:/plugins/sq/streams/*` title from inside the mindmap plugin felt confusingly scoped. Splitting it out keeps mindmap focused on mindmaps.

! Prerequisites

* TiddlyWiki ≥ 5.4.0
* `sq/streams` ≥ 1.2.24 — without it, this plugin sits idle (the override shadow exists but nothing ever renders it).
