"},"$:/plugins/rimir/streams-extras/readme":{"title":"$:/plugins/rimir/streams-extras/readme","type":"text/vnd.tiddlywiki","text":"! What it does

Adds a cascading ''Copy ▸'' / ''Paste ▸'' menu to `sq/streams`' right-click contextmenu. Lets you copy a stream node + its subtree as either a wiki-internal "structure" (round-trips losslessly) or as text in TiddlyWiki / Markdown / HTML outline format (copied to the system clipboard). Paste reads either source and creates fresh stream nodes under the right-clicked target.

! Key features

* ''Copy ▸ Structure'' — serialises the right-clicked node + its descendants (titles, text, hierarchy) into a TW state tiddler. Paste ▸ Structure recreates the subtree elsewhere with brand-new tiddler titles.
* ''Copy ▸ TW-List / MD-List / HTML-List'' — writes a flat outline to the system clipboard in the chosen format.
* ''Paste ▸ Structure'' — disabled unless the structure clipboard has content. Recreates the subtree as a new child of the right-clicked node.
* ''Paste ▸ Text-List'' — reads the clipboard, sniffs the format (TW `*` outline, Markdown indented `-`, or HTML `<ul><li>`), parses to a tree, creates matching child nodes under the target.
* ''Lineage stamp'' — every newly-pasted stream node carries an `orig-tiddler` field pointing at its source title (omitted for clipboard pastes — there's no source tiddler to record).
* ''Hover tooltips'' on every menu entry (including the stock streams entries — opt-in for custom contributions via `sq-contextmenu-tooltip`).
* ''Flatten in-place'' — the `$action-streams-flatten-inplace` widget collapses a streams subtree into a flat TW/MD/HTML outline appended to the root's text, then deletes the descendant nodes. Not exposed in the contextmenu; intended for callers that want to "freeze" a streams-note into a plain text/markdown/HTML note (e.g. `rimir/orga-apps` Hygiene panel).

! Prerequisites

* TiddlyWiki ≥ 5.4.0
* `sq/streams` ≥ 1.2.24

Without the streams plugin installed, this plugin is inert — its `$:/plugins/sq/streams/contextmenu/contextmenu-template` override stays in the shadow store but never renders anywhere.

! Quick start

Install the plugin, restart the wiki, then right-click any streams node. The cascading entries appear at the bottom of the contextmenu (above the Keyboard Shortcuts row).

! How it works

This is a shadow-override of streams' `contextmenu-template`, scoped via `plugin-priority: 2` so it wins shadow precedence over the streams plugin (which ships at priority 1). Inside the override, ''`Copy ▸`'' / ''`Paste ▸`'' entries are wrapped in `<div class="tc-popup-keep">` so clicking them flips the menu into sub-mode rather than dismissing the popup. The sub-mode is stored on the streams contextmenu state tiddler (`mode` field) and cleared automatically by an override of `oncontext-menu-actions` on each fresh right-click.

The actual copy/serialize/paste/parse work happens in four JS action widgets (`$action-streams-copy-structure`, `$action-streams-copy-list`, `$action-streams-paste-structure`, `$action-streams-paste-list`). The list format generator walks the `stream-list` field recursively; the paste path creates new stream-nodes via `wiki.generateNewTitle(<target>/node-<ts>)`, adding the parent to the wiki before recursing into descendants so sibling titles don't collide.
